# system-crew

This project uses **system-crew**: a 4-role workflow to design, implement, and verify game systems from user descriptions, reference content (videos, games, articles), playtest feedback, and design constraints.

## Roles

- **Producer** — intake, request type, ceremony (`quick`/`standard`/`full`), similarity (`faithful`/`inspired`), scope, routing
- **Systems Analyst** — break down references into evidence-backed briefs + specs; tuning parameter spaces; feedback issue cards; ideation design spaces
- **Implementer** — code the approved vertical slice, runtime-verified (`DONE`)
- **Fidelity QA** — converge check + compare result to reference + approved spec (readonly separate context preferred)

Canonical role docs live in the submodule: `.cursor/system-crew/roles/`
Workflow: `.cursor/system-crew/workflows/from-reference.md` (+ `tuning.md`, `feedback.md`, `ideation.md`)
Templates: `.cursor/system-crew/templates/`

## Default behavior

1. Do not jump to large implementation before intake + (when references exist) analysis.
2. Prefer one system / one vertical slice per pass. Producer sets `Ceremony`: `quick` (one `quick.md` + INDEX row), `standard` (asset/brief/spec/fidelity), `full` (Stages).
3. If one prompt mixes different kinds of work (analyze / idea eval / implement / QA, multiple slices, or multiple request types), split into Stages and run only the current Stage.
4. If the request is outside the protocol (agent skill/rule authoring, tooling-only, everyday fixes with no reference/metric/feedback intent), Producer declines the 4-role loop and reroutes — do not force `docs/references/` assets.
5. Mark guesses as hypotheses; every high-signal number in a brief points to an Evidence ledger row (`Ev#` with Method `seen | frame-step | tool | doc | hypothesis` and Confidence). LLMs label video segments; frame counting is a documented `frame-step` procedure run by a human or host tool. Hitstop needs 2+ signals. Juice intensity has no measurement standard — hypothesis only.
6. Specs are agent-consumable: success criteria in EARS form, statechart table when 3+ states, tunables mapped to Sheet/SO fields.
7. When the user names a role, follow that role file strictly. When unclear, start as Producer.
8. Persist reference work under `docs/references/` (INDEX + asset folder or `quick.md`). Capture **user callouts** separately. Asset Status: `draft | spec-draft | approved | implemented | verified | archived | archived-exp | living`. See `.cursor/system-crew/workflows/reference-assets.md`.
9. When the user proposes a system/implementation **idea** and asks to judge/apply it, run `.cursor/system-crew/workflows/idea-evaluation.md` first (Feasibility / Direction fit / Efficiency). Do not apply on taste alone. Log under `docs/decisions/ideas/`. Verdicts: `ADOPT` | `ADOPT_WITH_CHANGES` | `DEFER` | `REJECT`. `REJECT` is product-adoption rejection; time-boxed experiment retries need a fresh verdict. Competing visual trials use per-approach `exp/*` branches; product merge waits for a separate `ADOPT*`.
10. Request types beyond `reference`: `tuning` (numeric adjustment with a machine-checkable metric, parameter space, iteration budget → `docs/decisions/tuning/`), `feedback` (playtest feedback → issue cards with Observed/Expected/Unchanged → `docs/decisions/feedback/`), `ideation` (constrained design space + N variants; the **user** selects → `docs/decisions/ideation/`). Never delegate "is it fun" to the agent.
11. Role status codes are mandatory at hand-off: Analyst `READY | NEEDS_CALLOUT | BLOCKED`; Implementer `DONE | BLOCKED | NEEDS_SPEC` (no `DONE_UNVERIFIED`); QA `SHIPPABLE | NEEDS_FIX | NEEDS_SPEC | BLOCKED`.
12. Implementer closes verification at runtime before `DONE` (host Unity CLI first, then MCP, then editor Play; project Agent Playtest skills when available: realtime timeouts, short success evidence). Document how to reach the slice past title/intro gates. Discard ephemeral verification cheats/skips after the test. Agent Playtest/Webhook/Recorder porting alone is out_of_scope — host project workflows.
13. Fidelity QA runs a **converge check** (spec ↔ code/scene) before verdict, records evidence types (`runtime / screenshot / image-assert / telemetry / clip-pair / judge`), requires a clip pair for `faithful`, and uses LLM/VLM judges only for relative comparison. QA should run in a readonly separate context (`.cursor/agents/system-crew-fidelity-qa.md` when synced with `-EmitAgents`, else a fresh chat) — the implementing trajectory does not certify itself.
14. Approval gates batch questions and comments; after strategy approval, routine work (files, INDEX, runtime checks, per-card Stages) proceeds without re-asking. Re-ask only for scope expansion, hard-to-reverse changes, or spec conflicts.
15. If a **rag** knowledge repo is detectable (`RAG_ROOT`, sibling `../rag`, or `capture-to-rag` skill default path), after research / idea evaluation / meaningful asset close-out / tuning result / feedback resolution the Producer **offers** a capture-to-rag review. Do not force-save; do not replace host `docs/` logs. When capturing, follow the full `capture-to-rag` skill (file write + Discord via `DISCORD_RAG_WEBHOOK_URL`; never print the URL; never set webhook username/avatar).
16. When editing **this pack** (system-crew) with consumer-facing protocol changes: update `CHANGELOG.md`, bump `VERSION`, and if rag is detectable **automatically** run capture-to-rag (no review prompt) so other hosts can query "what to apply". Skip for typo-only / site copy-only edits.
17. Do not re-implement what the host already provides (plan mode, worktrees, best-of-n, subagents). The pack contributes game-domain checklists, asset conventions, and gates.

## Project-local overrides

Rules under `.cursor/rules/local/` override these for project-specific conventions only. Do not put shared crew protocol there.
